# Weapon-sprite SOURCE BMPs: 18 MB extracted, but compress to a 38 KB zip. Commit
# assets/weapons-src.zip (provenance); the extracted working dir is local-only.
# Regenerate the committed PNGs with `npm run assets:weapons`.
/assets/weapons-src/

# Local TLS certs for the docker nginx :443 mirror — machine-specific mkcert
# output (or a self-signed fallback), never committed. Generate per
# deploy/README.md → Friendly URL.
/data-server/certs/

# Sync-monitor CSVs. `soak-logs/` is an ad-hoc local pull-down for analysis and
# `logs/` is what sync-logger.js writes when run by hand. Raw capture, large (the
# 2026-06-28..08-02 soak is 131 MB across 36 files) and not worth permanent git
# history — this repo is cloned directly by Tony's LAN broadcast tooling.
#
# NOTE: ignored is not the same as safe. `git clean -xdf` deletes these, and the
# prod monitor that produced them is torn down, so that soak is NOT regenerable.
# It lives at d:/Git/_ktp-archive/hud-sync-soak-2026-06-28_2026-08-02.tar.gz.
# See e2e/repro/SYNC-MEASUREMENT.md → "Where the captured CSVs live".
/e2e/repro/soak-logs/
/e2e/repro/logs/
